n un tipo de servicio específico.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 39 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 9.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.5 to 6.2. December accounts for 38% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 23% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 7. Contract [1], for 14,999.98 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of awardees do not prove improper actions. These patterns could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing. Statistical trends alone do not indicate misconduct.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts to see if they align with budget cycles. Review awardee A’s contracts to determine if they repeat the same needs. Contract [1] shows a single high-value contract in December, which may reflect seasonal demand.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["l5J07lACiNPs%2BnLj3vAg5A%3D%3D","9b0umGm8%2FTv10HRJw8TEnQ%3D%3D","ecdlABAt3sIQyBAnWzHfCg%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}